THEOREM. Every 12-element integer set avoiding all arbitrary-distinct ordered solutions of
  x1 - 3*x2 + 3*x3 - x4 = 0
has span at least 50. Equivalently, every 12-subset of {0,...,49} contains a violation.

CERTIFIED SEMANTIC REDUCTION. If a<b<c<d and p=b-a, q=c-b, r=d-c, some ordering of these four values is a violation iff at least one holds:
  p+r=2q;
  p=3r or r=3p;
  p=2q+3r or r=2q+3p.
This is proved by expanding all 24 permutations, reducing to 12 primitive forms, rejecting seven by positivity, and pairing the five feasible forms by reflection.

CERTIFIED FINITE FACT. The exact hypergraph on 50 vertices has 15,560 forbidden supports. A 506-variable, 16,446-clause CNF is UNSAT. CaDiCaL, DRAT-trim, and lrat-check independently verified it. The LRAT is 98,504,857 bytes after trimming and is too large for practical Lean import on this machine.

EQUALITY DATA. At span 50, the unique normalized set is
  {0,3,5,7,10,23,27,40,43,45,47,50}
with gaps [3,2,2,3,13,4,13,3,2,2,3].

FAILED ROUTES. Direct bv_decide timed out at 900 seconds. Four alternate cardinality encodings produced larger LRAT files. Naive enumeration of all C3-free partial sets is too broad.

